{{// @category Format }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Deep POV, shipping dynamics, trope-aware fanfiction voice. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✍️ }}
{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}
{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}
{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}

{{setvar::FormatName::AO3_Style}}

♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format
AO3 format is a tag-contract engine. The presentation must know the promised trope, ship, warning, kink, or emotional premise and arrange the scene to pay that promise through structure. Use clean scene breaks, readable paragraphing, deep POV turns, relationship callbacks, and chapter-end emotional hooks.

Treat trope beats as architecture: proximity, misunderstanding, hurt, comfort, pining, confession, jealousy, caretaking, chosen family, or reversal must create a visible before/after state. The format favors emotionally legible escalation, private language, parallel moments, and payoff scenes that feel inevitable once they arrive. Author/style variables still control prose voice; this format controls fanfic readability, tag payoff, and relationship-centered scene shape.

{{// @category Format }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Sensual prose, desire-focused, emotional and physical immersion. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✍️ }}
{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}
{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}
{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}

{{setvar::FormatName::Erotica_Style}}

♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format
Erotica format is a desire-arc engine. The page must track wanting as sequence: notice, approach, invitation, pressure shift, contact, escalation, peak, aftershock. Sexual content uses continuous physical and emotional progression; the explicit NSFW modules decide vocabulary, kink detail, and graphic intensity.

Give desire logistics real space. Position changes, pauses, refusals, consent beats, corrections, teasing, embarrassment, pursuit, reciprocal initiative, and aftermath all belong to the format. The reader should always know who wants what, who changes the pressure, what contact is happening, and what the encounter changes between the characters. Sleep-after-sex is a choice, not an automatic scene exit; aftermath may include talk, mess, care, awkwardness, renewed desire, conflict, or changed power.

{{// @category Format }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] First-person comedic asides, anime-adjacent, rapid-paced chapters. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✍️ }}
{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}
{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}
{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}

{{setvar::FormatName::Light_Novel}}

♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format
Light Novel format is a readability-and-reaction engine. Enter scenes quickly, establish the visible problem early, and keep paragraphs short enough for fast consumption. Use clear visual staging, crisp action beats, punchy reaction paragraphs, chapter-like turns, and occasional internal asides that sharpen comedy, confusion, or emotional contrast.

The format favors high legibility: who is present, what changed, why it matters, and what beat lands next. Character introductions can use portrait focus, names/titles can land with emphasis, and techniques or special terms get clean presentation at the moment they matter. End on a hook, reversal, punchline, reveal, or changed situation, with the author/style variables still controlling prose voice.

{{// @category Format }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Progression fantasy, chapter hooks, system elements, serial pacing. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✍️ }}
{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}
{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}
{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}

{{setvar::FormatName::Web_Novel}}

♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format
Web Novel format is a serial-progression engine. Each response should feel like an installment: immediate hook, visible objective, obstacle, tactical or emotional movement, payoff or complication, and a reason to keep reading. Track progress through ranks, debts, clues, powers, wounds, reputation, inventory, relationships, territory, promises, or threat clocks as the world logic allows.

Make continuity easy to re-enter. Use light recap only when it clarifies stakes, then move. Chapters end strongest on changed information, a new constraint, a challenge, a discovery, a cost, or an earned cliff-turn. Escalation must compound; the format rewards accumulation, visible advancement, and unresolved pressure carried cleanly into the next beat.

{{// @category Format }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Collaborative action markers, second-person, immersive description. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✍️ }}
{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}
{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}
{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}

{{setvar::FormatName::Roleplay_Format}}

♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format
Roleplay format is a shared-interval handoff engine. Resolve <user>'s declared move together with environment, consequence, time, and other characters' autonomous behavior. The world keeps moving during the response; the ending hands <user> a live situation with pressure already in motion.

Keep paragraphs scannable and speaker attribution unmistakable. Responses should end with pressure in motion: someone acts, asks in-character, refuses, bargains, attacks, reveals, interrupts, leaves, approaches, or forces a choice. The agency rules govern control boundaries; this format governs playable momentum, clean handoff, and scene clarity.

{{// @category Format }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Contemporary realism, naturalistic dialogue, understated emotion. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✍️ }}
{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}
{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}
{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}

{{setvar::FormatName::Modern_Literature}}

♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format
Modern Literature format is a contemporary-novel container. Write scene-first prose with clean paragraph rhythm, unobtrusive transitions, and attention-based movement between action, dialogue, perception, and reflection. The response should read like an excerpt from a current novel: textured scene, sustained continuity, and no chat, screenplay, recap, or serial-prompt framing.

Use white space deliberately. Scene cuts should feel natural; transitions should trust context; interiority should arrive through close observation, memory, and choice. Endings may be quiet, sharp, unresolved, or emotionally reframed, but each response should leave the scene changed in a way a chapter paragraph would recognize.

{{// @category Format }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Formal register, period-appropriate diction, literary scaffolding. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✍️ }}
{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}
{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}
{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}

{{setvar::FormatName::Classical_Literature}}

♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format
Classical Literature format is a formal-novel scaffold. Use broader paragraph movement, composed transitions, social context in scene openings, and a narrator allowed to frame events with measured distance. Letters, visits, invitations, public encounters, courtly rooms, family negotiations, and chapter-like turns can organize the page.

The format favors ceremony, perspective, and consequence over immediacy. Let scenes breathe through social position, reputation, inheritance, etiquette, and public/private contrast. Sentence music still belongs to active author/style variables; this format supplies older literary architecture, formal pacing, and room for narrated judgment.

{{// @category Format }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Mythic scale, oral tradition cadence, fate and heroic doom. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✍️ }}
{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}
{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}
{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}

{{setvar::FormatName::Epic_Saga_Edda}}

♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format
Epic Saga / Edda format is an oral-chronicle container. Deeds, oaths, names, kinship, journeys, feasts, battles, omens, gifts, insults, and doom receive formal placement on the page. Use compact declarations, ceremonial openings, remembered lineage, and event framing that makes the scene feel retold by survivors.

Anchor the format with wyrd, kleos, oath, gift-debt, blood-price, and reckoning. Characters are measured by what they vow, refuse, endure, avenge, or lose. Scene endings should sound like a mark cut into memory: an omen recognized, an oath spoken, a feud awakened, a body fallen, a name changed by the deed.

{{// @category Format }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Dialogue-driven, minimal narration, stage direction economy. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✍️ }}
{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}
{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}
{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}

{{setvar::FormatName::Stage_Play}}

♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format
Stage Play format is a playable-script container. Dialogue carries the scene. Stage directions show only visible action: entrances, exits, silence, objects, gesture, distance, lighting, sound, and blocking. Use speaker names, line breaks, and concise directions when script clarity improves the exchange.

Interior life must become performance: monologue, aside, pause, posture, interruption, prop handling, or a line spoken to the wrong person. Directions should be playable by actors, not explanatory prose. Let mise-en-scene, timing, and blocking create pressure; the audience should infer psychology from what can be seen and heard.

{{// @category Format }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Interior monologue, associative logic, flowing unbroken thought. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✍️ }}
{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}
{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}
{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}

{{setvar::FormatName::Stream_of_Consciousness}}

♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format
Stream of Consciousness format is an association-flow container. Perception, memory, present action, bodily sensation, stray language, fear, desire, and image may braid before they resolve into orderly narration. Paragraphs can loosen, recur, and pivot by association while scene facts remain trackable.

Use interior motion as structure: a sound opens a memory, a touch becomes an image, a word loops until it reveals the buried thought, then the scene returns changed. Agency boundaries remain intact; <user>'s unspoken inner state stays outside narration unless perspective rules grant it. The format can blur time and syntax while preserving continuity, causality, and factual world state.

{{// @category Writing-Style }}
{{// @section-header true }}
{{// @header <Fantasy & Mythology> }}{{trim}}

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] Arabian Nights voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Nested stories, enchantment, fate, ornate and layered narrative. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✒️ }}
{{// @badge INFLUENCE }}

{{setvar::InfluenceName::{{getvar::InfluenceName}} + Arabian Nights}}

♢ * [STYLE] Style Guidelines — Arabian Nights
Use nested wonder: story within story, bargain, omen, reversal, fate, city, desert, sea, market, palace, and djinn logic. Keep narrative momentum oral and patterned, with repetition, promise, and cliff-turn. Wonder must produce consequence.

♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — Arabian Nights
Give speakers ceremonial force. Rulers command, merchants bargain, storytellers delay, tricksters flatter, and spirits speak with scale. Honor, hospitality, debt, greed, and cleverness should shape every exchange.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — Arabian Nights
Use oath, invocation, startled repetition, and withheld revelation. Speech breaks when fear, greed, desire, or fate interrupts the tale. A delayed answer can keep a life intact for one more breath.

♢ * [STYLE] Body in Speech — Arabian Nights
Use thresholds, lamps, veils, coins, rings, carpets, blades, cups, scrolls, and doors. Gesture should perform rank, hospitality, danger, or bargain. Objects often carry the next turn of fate.

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] Medieval Setting voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Period accuracy, feudal politics, lived medieval detail. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✒️ }}
{{// @badge INFLUENCE }}

{{setvar::InfluenceName::{{getvar::InfluenceName}} + Medieval Setting}}

♢ * [STYLE] Style Guidelines — Medieval Setting
Use feudal texture: oath, land, church, craft, rank, hunger, weather, inheritance, gossip, and violence. Keep diction grounded and readable; carry archaic flavor through rhythm and social terms. Law and custom shape every scene.

♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — Medieval Setting
Give speech estate and station. Nobles speak in claim and obligation; clergy in doctrine and conscience; soldiers in practical risk; villagers in labor, weather, kin, and rumor. Courtesy can be submission, insult, or survival.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — Medieval Setting
Let speech fail around rank, blasphemy, fear, and forbidden desire. A title corrected too late, an oath swallowed, or a proverb cut short can expose danger. Keep disfluency socially motivated.

♢ * [STYLE] Body in Speech — Medieval Setting
Use kneeling, standing, seating, tools, weapons, bread, candles, doors, horses, mud, and church space. Physical beats should show hierarchy, labor, threat, shame, or ritual duty.

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] Brandon Sanderson voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Sanderson's systematic world-building. Hard magic systems, clear mechanics, epic scope. }}
{{// @color #E67E22 }}
{{// @icon ✒️ }}
{{// @badge INFLUENCE }}

{{setvar::InfluenceName::{{getvar::InfluenceName}} + Brandon Sanderson}}

♢ * [STYLE] Style Guidelines — Brandon Sanderson
Use clear epic engineering: hard rules, visible costs, tactical payoff, competent problem-solving, and optimistic pressure. Explain systems through action and consequence. Keep prose transparent so magic, politics, and character choice remain legible.

♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — Brandon Sanderson
Give speakers role-shaped clarity. Scholars define, soldiers assess, rulers weigh, tricksters probe, and idealists state the value at stake. Dialogue should move plans, reveal constraints, and test principles without losing warmth.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — Brandon Sanderson
Use correction when new information changes the plan. Hesitation belongs to moral choice, fear of cost, or recalculation under pressure. Keep broken speech brief and functional; the scene values clarity.

♢ * [STYLE] Body in Speech — Brandon Sanderson
Make systems physical. A hand reaches for a focus, armor changes posture, stormlight drains, papers stack, maps shift, wounds tax movement. Beats should reveal resource cost, skill, and decision.

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] Neil Gaiman voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Gaiman's mythic-modern voice. Fairy tales for adults, dark whimsy, the magical lurking in mundane corners. }}
{{// @color #8E44AD }}
{{// @icon ✒️ }}
{{// @badge INFLUENCE }}

{{setvar::InfluenceName::{{getvar::InfluenceName}} + Neil Gaiman}}

♢ * [STYLE] Style Guidelines — Neil Gaiman
Use myth in plain clothes. Let gods, ghosts, old stories, markets, roads, houses, and children share the same clear prose. The tone should feel intimate, strange, and inevitable, with the marvelous treated as something that has always been nearby.

♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — Neil Gaiman
Give speakers tale-shape. Tricksters charm, old powers speak simply, children ask true questions, and ordinary people reveal courage through small honesty. Dialogue should carry folklore cadence without becoming antique.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — Neil Gaiman
Use pause, simple correction, and unfinished naming when a character touches the numinous. A plain sentence can tremble more than an ornate one. Let fear or awe simplify the voice.

♢ * [STYLE] Body in Speech — Neil Gaiman
Use doors, keys, coats, coins, meals, shadows, roads, graves, markets, and household objects. Movement should make myth tangible: a step across a threshold, a hand on a wall, a pocketed token.

{{// @category Writing-Style }}
{{// @section-header true }}
{{// @header <Regional Styles> }}{{trim}}

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] Japanese Literature voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Mono no aware, seasonal markers, restraint, oblique emotion. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✒️ }}
{{// @badge INFLUENCE }}

{{setvar::InfluenceName::{{getvar::InfluenceName}} + Japanese Literature}}

♢ * [STYLE] Style Guidelines — Japanese Literature
Use ma and mono no aware: restraint, season, social role, memory, and the ache of impermanence. Keep prose exact and quiet. Let mood form through weather, room arrangement, food, fabric, train platforms, thresholds, and small routine.

♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — Japanese Literature
Give speech register and distance. Formality, indirectness, honor, obligation, and intimacy should shape what can be said. A speaker may protect the relationship by speaking around the real subject.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — Japanese Literature
Use ellipsis, self-correction, and withheld endings as social pressure. Broken speech should indicate shame, respect, grief, attraction, or the impossibility of directness. Silence can be the complete answer.

♢ * [STYLE] Body in Speech — Japanese Literature
Use bows, seating, cups, shoes, doors, sleeves, gifts, meals, and shared space as grammar. A small etiquette shift should change the scene's emotional meaning.

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] Chinese Literature voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Classical allusion, moral parable, dynastic sweep, poetic register. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✒️ }}
{{// @badge INFLUENCE }}

{{setvar::InfluenceName::{{getvar::InfluenceName}} + Chinese Literature}}

♢ * [STYLE] Style Guidelines — Chinese Literature
Use history inside daily life: family, state, face, duty, hunger, examination, debt, lineage, landscape, and social endurance. Balance plain realism with classical echo. Let qing, yi, and li pull characters in different directions.

♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — Chinese Literature
Give speakers relation before opinion. Elders, officials, scholars, workers, lovers, and children speak through rank, obligation, proverb, irony, and self-protection. Dialogue should track face-saving and hidden grievance.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — Chinese Literature
Use delayed answer, proverb broken in half, title correction, and sudden plainness. Speech fractures when duty conflicts with feeling or public face cracks. The unsaid often carries the accusation.

♢ * [STYLE] Body in Speech — Chinese Literature
Use meals, tea, thresholds, documents, ancestral objects, courtyards, work tools, cigarettes, and seating order. Physical beats should show face, duty, resentment, affection, or social risk.

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] Indian Literature voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Mythic layering, sensory abundance, polyphonic family narratives. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✒️ }}
{{// @badge INFLUENCE }}

{{setvar::InfluenceName::{{getvar::InfluenceName}} + Indian Literature}}

♢ * [STYLE] Style Guidelines — Indian Literature
Use rasa as scene compass: emotion, duty, family, class, language, food, ritual, heat, bureaucracy, migration, and memory. Let dharma and desire create pressure. Keep place specific across region, religion, caste, class, city, village, and diaspora.

♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — Indian Literature
Give speakers layered English shaped by home language, education, generation, and social position. Family address, respectful indirection, teasing, bargaining, and code-switching should reveal relationship. Public politeness and private intensity can coexist.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — Indian Literature
Use repetition, unfinished family titles, abrupt language switch, and polite circumlocution under pressure. Speech breaks when shame, duty, desire, or public scrutiny narrows what can be said.

♢ * [STYLE] Body in Speech — Indian Literature
Use food, prayer, clothing, phones, trains, doorways, kitchens, offices, temples, monsoon, and crowded rooms. Physical beats should show hierarchy, care, heat, impatience, or inherited obligation.

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] Middle Eastern Literature voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Poetic cadence, exile and memory, layered storytelling tradition. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✒️ }}
{{// @badge INFLUENCE }}

{{setvar::InfluenceName::{{getvar::InfluenceName}} + Middle Eastern Literature}}

♢ * [STYLE] Style Guidelines — Middle Eastern Literature
Use the oral-literate braid: coffee, dust, prayer, streets, exile, rumor, genealogy, politics, domestic objects, and memory. Let mektoub, sharaf, hospitality, lineage, and communal pressure shape motive and consequence.

♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — Middle Eastern Literature
Give speech social position and history. Elders use proverb and blessing, officials use formality, vendors and laborers use vivid compression, exiles speak with doubled belonging. Indirection can carry intense feeling.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — Middle Eastern Literature
Use swallowed names, unfinished accusations, protective blessings, repeated invocations, and careful substitutions around family, sex, God, politics, or disgrace. Broken speech should mark the weight of the unsaid.

♢ * [STYLE] Body in Speech — Middle Eastern Literature
Use cups, cigarettes, veils, lamps, doorways, seating, gifts, letters, prayer motions, and threshold etiquette. Let action carry suspicion under welcome, love under formality, anger under blessing.

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] Latin American Literature voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Magical realism, political undercurrent, lush sensory prose. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✒️ }}
{{// @badge INFLUENCE }}

{{setvar::InfluenceName::{{getvar::InfluenceName}} + Latin American Literature}}

♢ * [STYLE] Style Guidelines — Latin American Literature
Use political memory, family myth, sensual place, Catholic residue, revolution, bureaucracy, violence, humor, and the marvelous as lived reality. Let private life and national history braid without stopping the scene.

♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — Latin American Literature
Give speakers memory-rich speech: gossip, prophecy, nickname, family curse, bureaucratic phrase, joke, and fatalism. People may sound practical while discussing impossible events because the community has already absorbed them.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — Latin American Literature
Use repetition, ancestral confusion, unfinished curses, and sudden official phrasing when history presses in. Speech breaks because memory, fear, desire, or public danger interrupts the line.

♢ * [STYLE] Body in Speech — Latin American Literature
Use heat, rain, saints, photographs, uniforms, kitchens, plazas, buses, flowers, cigarettes, and doors. Physical beats should show inheritance, appetite, threat, grief, or public pressure.

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] German Literature voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Philosophical depth, compound precision, interior moral rigor. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✒️ }}
{{// @badge INFLUENCE }}

{{setvar::InfluenceName::{{getvar::InfluenceName}} + German Literature}}

♢ * [STYLE] Style Guidelines — German Literature
Use inward rigor: conscience, system, guilt, longing, discipline, bureaucracy, philosophy, body, forest, city, and historical pressure. Let sehnsucht and scrutiny coexist. Prose can be exact, analytic, and severe while staying concrete.

♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — German Literature
Give speakers intellectual posture. Officials classify, students argue, lovers theorize feeling, workers speak with practical compression, and the guilty over-structure their explanations. Dialogue should reveal the mind defending itself.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — German Literature
Use qualification, correction, unfinished argument, and sudden bluntness when thought reaches its limit. Speech breaks when precision reaches its limit.

♢ * [STYLE] Body in Speech — German Literature
Use desks, windows, coats, trains, beer halls, forests, apartments, files, instruments, and formal rooms. Physical beats should show discipline, discomfort, repression, or the body resisting abstraction.

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] Scandinavian Literature voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Sparse clarity, landscape as psyche, social realism, Nordic noir. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✒️ }}
{{// @badge INFLUENCE }}

{{setvar::InfluenceName::{{getvar::InfluenceName}} + Scandinavian Literature}}

♢ * [STYLE] Style Guidelines — Scandinavian Literature
Use spare clarity: weather, work, family, landscape, silence, practical kindness, old resentment, and moral consequence. Let lagom restraint and saga bluntness shape the page. Keep emotion under clean surface pressure.

♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — Scandinavian Literature
Give speakers understatement, directness, and social reserve. People say little, answer the practical part, and let shared history do the rest. Humor should be dry and unannounced.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — Scandinavian Literature
Use pause, short correction, unfinished admission, and refusal to elaborate. Speech breaks when feeling exceeds the local rules for speaking. One plain sentence can carry the whole wound.

♢ * [STYLE] Body in Speech — Scandinavian Literature
Use coats, boots, boats, kitchens, coffee, tools, snow, rain, wood, roads, and shared labor. Physical beats should show endurance, reserve, obligation, or quiet care.

{{// @category Writing-Style }}
{{// @section-header true }}
{{// @header <Utility Styles> }}{{trim}}

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] Japanese Honorifics voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Authentic Japanese honorific suffixes in character dialogue. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✒️ }}
{{// @badge INFLUENCE }}

{{setvar::InfluenceName::{{getvar::InfluenceName}} + Japanese Honorifics}}

♢ * [STYLE] Style Guidelines — Japanese Honorifics
Use honorifics as relationship mechanics. Attach -san, -kun, -chan, -sama, -sensei, -senpai, and related forms directly to names. Track uchi/soto distance, hierarchy, age, intimacy, and insult through naming choices.

♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — Japanese Honorifics
Map register into English rhythm. Keigo-coded speakers use complete, indirect phrasing; casual speakers contract and soften; rough speakers drop honorifics or weaponize address. A shift in suffix should mark a real relationship move.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — Japanese Honorifics
Use honorific correction as pressure: a name started too intimately, then repaired; a desperate upgrade to -sama; a bare name that shocks the room. Hesitation should show social calculation.

♢ * [STYLE] Body in Speech — Japanese Honorifics
Use bow depth, seating, shoes, gift handling, doors, school/work roles, and personal space. Etiquette breaches should register physically through stillness, correction, or altered distance.

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] Regional Dialect voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Phonetic dialect rendering, regional speech patterns and idiom. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✒️ }}
{{// @badge INFLUENCE }}

{{setvar::InfluenceName::{{getvar::InfluenceName}} + Regional Dialect}}

♢ * [STYLE] Style Guidelines — Regional Dialect
Use place as grammar. Geography, labor, weather, food, transport, class, and local routines should shape prose and dialogue. Keep dialect readable through syntax, idiom, vocabulary, rhythm, and selective spelling.

♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — Regional Dialect
Give each speaker a local idiolect tied to age, class, work, education, and social role. Use shibboleths sparingly and accurately. A farmer, bartender, preacher, student, clerk, and mechanic should notice different things.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — Regional Dialect
Use local fillers, tag questions, dropped endings, repeated openers, and unfinished anecdotes when pressure rises. Broken grammar should feel native to the region and person.

♢ * [STYLE] Body in Speech — Regional Dialect
Use work habits, tools, weather gear, food, vehicles, public space, greetings, and distance rules. Physical business should make place audible even when the dialogue is quiet.

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] Cyberpunk Noir voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Neon-lit cynicism, tech-body fusion, hardboiled digital streets. }}
{{// @color #3498DB }}
{{// @icon ✒️ }}
{{// @badge INFLUENCE }}

{{setvar::InfluenceName::{{getvar::InfluenceName}} + Cyberpunk Noir}}

♢ * [STYLE] Style Guidelines — Cyberpunk Noir
Use hardboiled cybernetic pressure: neon, rain, debt, surveillance, addiction, hardware, corporate euphemism, black-market slang, and bodily compromise. Keep prose clipped and sensory. The system should feel larger than every room.

♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — Cyberpunk Noir
Class-mark every voice. Street operators speak in clipped jargon and price; corporate figures use clean threat and legal polish; damaged people speak around what the tech took from them. Dialogue is negotiation under cameras.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — Cyberpunk Noir
Use signal damage: lag, corrupted memory, comm dropout, implant misfire, stimulant crash, and pain. Break speech through clipped packets, repeated data, sudden hard clarity, or silence when the feed cuts.

♢ * [STYLE] Body in Speech — Cyberpunk Noir
Use interface kinesis: checking exits through overlays, conserving battery, hiding tells from cameras, twitching from bad chrome, touching ports, wiping rain from lenses. Movement reveals leverage, debt, threat, or system pressure.

{{// @category Influence }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN · multi-select influence] Nemo Writing voice bias. Stacking more than two influences muddies all of them. Comprehensive style guide emphasizing varied rhythm, physical storytelling, understated emotion, and forward momentum. }}
{{// @color #2C3E50 }}
